<urn:atm:triage:finding/RBP-F101>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBP-F101" ;
  triage:title "Task-path rejection families share one generic AtmErrorCode instead of one code per family" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr BA-PHASE-END-QA @ 9f5aef2fe (report PR #1418 comment 5644355381). Finding: the task rejection paths (third-party close, stale counterparty, already-closed, peer-resolution failure, etc.) do not each carry a distinct AtmErrorCode -- callers and tests cannot discriminate which rejection family fired from the error code alone. fenix's ruling: one AtmErrorCode per rejection family, additive (no breaking change), with a corresponding ADR-061 row. Routed to arch-ctm fix/phase-ba-review-2 (item 14, in progress). Related to CPR-020's anyhow-flattening defect (same symptom, different layer)." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "error-handling" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T07:08:18Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
